# POS register scan vs product picker (do not regress)

On the register check search field, a barcode/КМ scan must **not** open the product list over the receipt. Slow POS-monitor scanners often exceed the 80 ms wedge gap.

## Invariants

1. `nextRegisterScanBurst` / `looksLikeRegisterScanInput`: digit-only codes and marking/GS1-shaped input hide the picker even when inter-char gap > 80 ms.
2. Once a burst/scan-shaped session started, keep `burst` while the value keeps growing (sticky), until the field is cleared.
3. When `search` is cleared after a successful scan (bypassing `handleSearchChange`), reset the burst ref so the next manual name search can open the picker.

## Do not

- Rely only on `REGISTER_SCAN_GAP_MS` for POS Bluetooth scanners.
- Open the register picker for digit-only / КМ input that is still growing.
